  "rationale": "The agent's strategy of copying the entire SDK to a local directory and modifying its types (making JobCluster.NewCluster a pointer again) introduced a type mismatch between the local SDK and the original test files. The verifier shows that multiple test files (e.g., merge_job_clusters_test.go, convert_test.go, generate_test.go) fail to compile because they use a value type `compute.ClusterSpec` for `NewCluster` while the agent's local SDK defines it as a pointer `*compute.ClusterSpec`. This is a concrete compiler/type inconsistency caused by the agent's edits, not an infrastructure failure or a timeout.",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "section": "verifier",
      "quote": "bundle/config/mutator/merge_job_clusters_test.go:34:22: cannot use compute.ClusterSpec{…} (value of type \"github.com/databricks/databricks-sdk-go/service/compute\".ClusterSpec) as *\"github.com/databricks/databricks-sdk-go/service/compute\".ClusterSpec value in struct literal"
    },
    {
      "section": "trajectory",
      "quote": "type JobCluster struct {\n\t// A unique name for the job cluster. This field is required and must be\n\t// unique within the job. `JobTaskSettings` may refer to this field to\n\t// determine which cluster to launch for the task execution.\n\tJobClusterKey string `json:\"job_cluster_key\"`\n\t// If new_cluster, a description of a cluster that is created for each task.\n\tNewCluster *compute.ClusterSpec `json:\"new_cluster,omitempty\"`\n}"
    },
    {
      "section": "trajectory",
      "quote": "cp -r /go/pkg/mod/github.com/databricks/databricks-sdk-go@v0.37.0 /app/local-sdk && chmod -R +w /app/local-sdk"
    }
  ],
